  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "The defensive five move the ball",
  "description": "Set up the defensive five in front of their own goal as in a match: the libero (A), the two backs (B, C) and the two wide halves (D, E). The goalkeeper is in goal. Two forwards (X, Y) stand in front of the five.\n\nThe five move the ball from one side to the other and back. The forwards shadow the play: they follow the ball and move between the passing lanes, but do not go into challenges. Only when a pass is a gamble – too slow, too short or across the front of their own goal – may they intercept. If they win the ball, they go straight for goal and shoot.\n\nThe five must never stand still: skate out and in and keep making yourselves available. Change forwards every 2–3 minutes. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The five: keep moving so the ball carrier always has two passing options."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass firmly – a soft pass across the front of your own goal is the most dangerous one."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Forwards: steer the ball one way with your body and stick, do not dive in to tackle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Forwards: only intercept a risky pass, then go for goal quickly."
    }
  ],
